    "resource_bounds": "The source applies a 95 MiB address-space limit, fixed CPU/alarm bounds, bounded 8 MiB semantic reads, sequential per-cohort materialization and explicit refusal of the 25,193,469-byte formatter member for semantic parsing. The separate earlier streaming stage admits that member's bytes.",
    "failure_preservation": "Any validation exception leaves passed false. The first AST mismatch source and result are preserved; v2 does not alter original record bytes.",
    "primary_source": {
      "url": "https://docs.python.org/3.13/library/ast.html#ast.dump",
      "claim": "Python 3.13 ast.dump exposes show_empty; false omits optional empty lists. Exact equality for these recorded sources is established by the bound reader result, not a universal cross-version AST equivalence claim."
    },
